AB  - While simulated story worlds have proven to be fertile ground for emergent storytelling in research and in commercial game genres such as life simulation, 4X, and roguelikes, they have also proven challenging to create. Building these simulations can involve hand-authoring large amounts of content that provide context for character decision-making, ensure variation among generated narratives, and align with the simulation’s narrative setting and themes. This short paper discusses preliminary work on leveraging ChatGPT to generate theme-relevant content for Neighborly, a character-driven settlement simulation framework designed for narrative generation. Given a textual description of the narrative setting, we demonstrate how ChatGPT can be used to generate Python code for characters’ businesses, occupations, and traits. We discuss challenges with development and future work. © 2023 Copyright for this paper by its authors.
